&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Meryl Sole:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr. Meryl Sole, Ed. D. teaches undergraduate and graduate courses in music education at New York University and Teachers College, Columbia University. She is an active researcher who focuses on the musical lives of toddlers, musical parenting, and popular music education. She has co-authored two books, Knowing the Children We Teach: Essays on Music Learning (2023) and Seeking the Mystical Child: Nurturing Young Children&amp;#39;s Identity, Faith, and Belief (in press).&lt;/p&gt;
