&lt;p&gt;Join us in March when NECR program director Dr. Beth Fisher-Yoshida discusses negotiation with Visiting Scholar.Julia Vassileva.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
The webinar discusses Julia&amp;rsquo;s research, which investigates the low levels of women&amp;rsquo;s inclusion in peace negotiations in post-Soviet states, focusing on conflicts in regions such as Abkhazia, South Ossetia, Nagorno-Karabakh, and Transnistria. Based on fieldwork she conducted in Georgia, Azerbaijan, Armenia, and Moldova (over 120 interviews), it highlights the unique challenges women face in these high-stakes negotiations. The research comes amid global rising tensions, particularly after Russia&amp;rsquo;s invasion of Ukraine, which has highlighted unresolved conflicts in post-Soviet Eastern Europe. The work seeks to bridge theory and practice by detailing the barriers to women&amp;rsquo;s participation, and it speaks to the importance of ensuring more effective, sustainable, and inclusive peace negotiations in the region and beyond.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This event will be held online. The link to join virtually will be provided upon registration.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
